{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTUYkHbxcVfHKXQ7ET7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PwbtPi1NX1nYYJAvY2hfxD","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/README.md","old_string":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","new_string":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block one is the\nstatic coaching rules (byte-identical for every athlete and day); block two is the\nper-athlete tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). A `save_fact` write\nonly evicts block two, so the rules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read from cache."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1440,"cache_read_input_tokens":35215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1440},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ec9b1df-cd5d-414f-8b21-83b2200d6a92","uuid":"01233ed9-ceda-4b3e-b084-9a849a6749e8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:27:34.849Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTUYaMq9rSymdvMCWad","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PwbtPi1NX1nYYJAvY2hfxD":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/README.md","old_string":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","new_string":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block one is the\nstatic coaching rules (byte-identical for every athlete and day); block two is the\nper-athlete tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). A `save_fact` write\nonly evicts block two, so the rules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read from cache."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PwbtPi1NX1nYYJAvY2hfxD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ec9b1df-cd5d-414f-8b21-83b2200d6a92","uuid":"09afd0e3-0b21-4685-b59d-a4736f845892","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:27:34.873Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/README.md","oldString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block one is the\nstatic coaching rules (byte-identical for every athlete and day); block two is the\nper-athlete tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). A `save_fact` write\nonly evicts block two, so the rules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read from cache.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":5,"newStart":12,"newLines":8,"lines":[" messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`)."," Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+prompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block one is the","+static coaching rules (byte-identical for every athlete and day); block two is the","+per-athlete tail (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). A `save_fact` write","+only evicts block two, so the rules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up","+messages inside the 5-minute window read from cache."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PwbtPi1NX1nYYJAvY2hfxD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtTUYkHbxcVfHKXQ7ET7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P3FvmLT5TrcAxA31xRNx9K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: a `save_fact` write no longer evicts the static instructions\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` returned one text block containing `INSTRUCTIONS` plus\n`athlete_context()` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language), with a single\n`cache_control` marker at the end. The prompt cache is a prefix hash, so any byte\nchange inside that block misses the whole block. Every `save_fact` rewrites the\nfacts list, which changes the block, which re-caches the ~1000 tokens of\ninstructions too. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`: the call right\nafter a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a full\n`cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, unmodified text. It contains no interpolated values, so it is\n   byte-identical across athletes, days and memory writes.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`: everything per-athlete and volatile.\n\nA memory write changes only block 2. Block 1 stays cached. Two of Anthropic's\nfour allowed markers are used. `build_request`, `select_tools`, the tools array\nand the message loop are unchanged.\n\n`README.md` (the caching paragraph) is updated to describe the two blocks.\n\n## Verification done\n\n- Ran `build_system` in a local script: block 1 is identical for two athletes,\n  for a different date, and after a `save_fact` (`assert` passed). Block 2\n  changes on a date change and on a memory write. Both blocks carry the\n  ephemeral marker.\n- The module imports and compiles without the SDK installed.\n\n**Not verified:** no real API call was made. There is no key in this session, and\na live call costs money and is outward-facing, so I did not make one. The check\nthat settles it is the one in the colleague note: after a `save_fact`, the next\ncall should show `cache_read_input_tokens` covering block 1 and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` near the size of block 2 only (~60 tokens of\ncontext plus the date line). If `cache_creation` is still about the whole prompt,\nsee the caveat below.\n\n## Caveats (please read)\n\n1. **Minimum cacheable size.** The API only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens\n   for Sonnet (`claude-sonnet-4-5`). The prefix up to block 1 is the tools array\n   plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. Calibrating against the logged numbers (the old\n   single-block request was 1046 tokens for 3111 characters, about 3 characters\n   per token), a simple message with only the two core tools comes to roughly\n   980 tokens. In that case the block-1 marker is silently ignored and block 2's\n   marker caches the whole prefix, which is the old behaviour. Messages that\n   also pull in the `plan` or `race` tool group are larger and should clear the\n   minimum, but that is borderline by my estimate. This needs the real `usage`\n   numbers to confirm. I did not pad the prompt to get over the minimum, because\n   that would be adding content to the coaching instructions, which is your call.\n   Options if the check fails: add real static content (for example, fuller\n   coaching rules), or always send the full tool set (costs more tokens on simple\n   messages, the trade the keyword filter was made to avoid).\n\n2. **Tool filtering still shares the prefix.** The tools array sits above the\n   system prompt, so a message that contains `plan`, `race` and similar words\n   changes the tools prefix and misses block 1 as well. Within one message's tool\n   loop the tools are constant, so this only costs once per such message. It is\n   not a memory-write problem, so I left it alone.\n\n3. **Date is in block 2.** Block 2 changes once per day as well as on memory\n   writes. That is intended: the tail is small (~60 tokens).\n\n## Colleague note: what applied\n\n- **Applied:** two `cache_control: ephemeral` markers, one static block and one\n  volatile tail. A memory write re-caches only the tail. Static block kept\n  byte-stable (no interpolated values). Verify steps adapted to usage fields.\n- **Applied as a principle, nothing to change:** the tools array and everything\n  above the system prompt should stay byte-stable. The tool groups are in a fixed\n  order, and the tools are not reordered. The filter itself is unchanged (caveat 2).\n- **Applied as a check:** the per-message selection warning. This code has no\n  top-N fact selection. All facts are always loaded, so the tail is not\n  personalised per message.\n- **Not applied:** \"rarest-changing first\" ordering inside block 2. Within one\n  cache entry, order doesn't change what gets evicted, so I kept the existing\n  field order. Splitting block 2 further would use more markers for little gain.\n- **Not applicable:** the Telegram details, the coach-bot content, and the\n  specific token counts. Those are that project's numbers, not this one's.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1440,"cache_read_input_tokens":35215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1440},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ec9b1df-cd5d-414f-8b21-83b2200d6a92","uuid":"83f23837-4a63-43ca-98d7-74514acd5dc0","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:27:42.980Z","request_id":"req_011CgtTUYaMq9rSymdvMCWad","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01P3FvmLT5TrcAxA31xRNx9K":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: a `save_fact` write no longer evicts the static instructions\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` returned one text block containing `INSTRUCTIONS` plus\n`athlete_context()` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language), with a single\n`cache_control` marker at the end. The prompt cache is a prefix hash, so any byte\nchange inside that block misses the whole block. Every `save_fact` rewrites the\nfacts list, which changes the block, which re-caches the ~1000 tokens of\ninstructions too. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`: the call right\nafter a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a full\n`cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, unmodified text. It contains no interpolated values, so it is\n   byte-identical across athletes, days and memory writes.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`: everything per-athlete and volatile.\n\nA memory write changes only block 2. Block 1 stays cached. Two of Anthropic's\nfour allowed markers are used. `build_request`, `select_tools`, the tools array\nand the message loop are unchanged.\n\n`README.md` (the caching paragraph) is updated to describe the two blocks.\n\n## Verification done\n\n- Ran `build_system` in a local script: block 1 is identical for two athletes,\n  for a different date, and after a `save_fact` (`assert` passed). Block 2\n  changes on a date change and on a memory write. Both blocks carry the\n  ephemeral marker.\n- The module imports and compiles without the SDK installed.\n\n**Not verified:** no real API call was made. There is no key in this session, and\na live call costs money and is outward-facing, so I did not make one. The check\nthat settles it is the one in the colleague note: after a `save_fact`, the next\ncall should show `cache_read_input_tokens` covering block 1 and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` near the size of block 2 only (~60 tokens of\ncontext plus the date line). If `cache_creation` is still about the whole prompt,\nsee the caveat below.\n\n## Caveats (please read)\n\n1. **Minimum cacheable size.** The API only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens\n   for Sonnet (`claude-sonnet-4-5`). The prefix up to block 1 is the tools array\n   plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. Calibrating against the logged numbers (the old\n   single-block request was 1046 tokens for 3111 characters, about 3 characters\n   per token), a simple message with only the two core tools comes to roughly\n   980 tokens. In that case the block-1 marker is silently ignored and block 2's\n   marker caches the whole prefix, which is the old behaviour. Messages that\n   also pull in the `plan` or `race` tool group are larger and should clear the\n   minimum, but that is borderline by my estimate. This needs the real `usage`\n   numbers to confirm. I did not pad the prompt to get over the minimum, because\n   that would be adding content to the coaching instructions, which is your call.\n   Options if the check fails: add real static content (for example, fuller\n   coaching rules), or always send the full tool set (costs more tokens on simple\n   messages, the trade the keyword filter was made to avoid).\n\n2. **Tool filtering still shares the prefix.** The tools array sits above the\n   system prompt, so a message that contains `plan`, `race` and similar words\n   changes the tools prefix and misses block 1 as well. Within one message's tool\n   loop the tools are constant, so this only costs once per such message. It is\n   not a memory-write problem, so I left it alone.\n\n3. **Date is in block 2.** Block 2 changes once per day as well as on memory\n   writes. That is intended: the tail is small (~60 tokens).\n\n## Colleague note: what applied\n\n- **Applied:** two `cache_control: ephemeral` markers, one static block and one\n  volatile tail. A memory write re-caches only the tail. Static block kept\n  byte-stable (no interpolated values). Verify steps adapted to usage fields.\n- **Applied as a principle, nothing to change:** the tools array and everything\n  above the system prompt should stay byte-stable. The tool groups are in a fixed\n  order, and the tools are not reordered. The filter itself is unchanged (caveat 2).\n- **Applied as a check:** the per-message selection warning. This code has no\n  top-N fact selection. All facts are always loaded, so the tail is not\n  personalised per message.\n- **Not applied:** \"rarest-changing first\" ordering inside block 2. Within one\n  cache entry, order doesn't change what gets evicted, so I kept the existing\n  field order. Splitting block 2 further would use more markers for little gain.\n- **Not applicable:** the Telegram details, the coach-bot content, and the\n  specific token counts. Those are that project's numbers, not this one's.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3FvmLT5TrcAxA31xRNx9K","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/ANSWER.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ec9b1df-cd5d-414f-8b21-83b2200d6a92","uuid":"37e0943a-84ff-4352-85a7-e2619ffb2012","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:27:43.011Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/h-cIXTxI/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: a `save_fact` write no longer evicts the static instructions\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` returned one text block containing `INSTRUCTIONS` plus\n`athlete_context()` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language), with a single\n`cache_control` marker at the end. The prompt cache is a prefix hash, so any byte\nchange inside that block misses the whole block. Every `save_fact` rewrites the\nfacts list, which changes the block, which re-caches the ~1000 tokens of\ninstructions too. That matches `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`: the call right\nafter a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a full\n`cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)\n\nThe system prompt is now two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, unmodified text. It contains no interpolated values, so it is\n   byte-identical across athletes, days and memory writes.\n2. `athlete_context(a, today)`: everything per-athlete and volatile.\n\nA memory write changes only block 2. Block 1 stays cached. Two of Anthropic's\nfour allowed markers are used. `build_request`, `select_tools`, the tools array\nand the message loop are unchanged.\n\n`README.md` (the caching paragraph) is updated to describe the two blocks.\n\n## Verification done\n\n- Ran `build_system` in a local script: block 1 is identical for two athletes,\n  for a different date, and after a `save_fact` (`assert` passed). Block 2\n  changes on a date change and on a memory write. Both blocks carry the\n  ephemeral marker.\n- The module imports and compiles without the SDK installed.\n\n**Not verified:** no real API call was made. There is no key in this session, and\na live call costs money and is outward-facing, so I did not make one. The check\nthat settles it is the one in the colleague note: after a `save_fact`, the next\ncall should show `cache_read_input_tokens` covering block 1 and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` near the size of block 2 only (~60 tokens of\ncontext plus the date line). If `cache_creation` is still about the whole prompt,\nsee the caveat below.\n\n## Caveats (please read)\n\n1. **Minimum cacheable size.** The API only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens\n   for Sonnet (`claude-sonnet-4-5`). The prefix up to block 1 is the tools array\n   plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. Calibrating against the logged numbers (the old\n   single-block request was 1046 tokens for 3111 characters, about 3 characters\n   per token), a simple message with only the two core tools comes to roughly\n   980 tokens. In that case the block-1 marker is silently ignored and block 2's\n   marker caches the whole prefix, which is the old behaviour. Messages that\n   also pull in the `plan` or `race` tool group are larger and should clear the\n   minimum, but that is borderline by my estimate. This needs the real `usage`\n   numbers to confirm. I did not pad the prompt to get over the minimum, because\n   that would be adding content to the coaching instructions, which is your call.\n   Options if the check fails: add real static content (for example, fuller\n   coaching rules), or always send the full tool set (costs more tokens on simple\n   messages, the trade the keyword filter was made to avoid).\n\n2. **Tool filtering still shares the prefix.** The tools array sits above the\n   system prompt, so a message that contains `plan`, `race` and similar words\n   changes the tools prefix and misses block 1 as well. Within one message's tool\n   loop the tools are constant, so this only costs once per such message. It is\n   not a memory-write problem, so I left it alone.\n\n3. **Date is in block 2.** Block 2 changes once per day as well as on memory\n   writes. That is intended: the tail is small (~60 tokens).\n\n## Colleague note: what applied\n\n- **Applied:** two `cache_control: ephemeral` markers, one static block and one\n  volatile tail. A memory write re-caches only the tail. Static block kept\n  byte-stable (no interpolated values). Verify steps adapted to usage fields.\n- **Applied as a principle, nothing to change:** the tools array and everything\n  above the system prompt should stay byte-stable. The tool groups are in a fixed\n  order, and the tools are not reordered. The filter itself is unchanged (caveat 2).\n- **Applied as a check:** the per-message selection warning. This code has no\n  top-N fact selection. All facts are always loaded, so the tail is not\n  personalised per message.\n- **Not applied:** \"rarest-changing first\" ordering inside block 2. Within one\n  cache entry, order doesn't change what gets evicted, so I kept the existing\n  field order. Splitting block 2 further would use more markers for little gain.\n- **Not applicable:** the Telegram details, the coach-bot content, and the\n  specific token counts. Those are that project's numbers, not this one's.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P3FvmLT5TrcAxA31xRNx9K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
